<h1>average case</h1>
<p>
(definition)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
Having to do with the mathematical average of all cases.
</p>

<p>
<strong>See also</strong>
<a href="bestcase.html"><em>best case</em></a>, <a href="worstcase.html"><em>worst case</em></a>, <a href="mean.html"><em>mean</em></a>, <a href="mode.html"><em>mode</em></a>, <a href="median.html"><em>median</em></a>.
</p>

<p>
<em>Note:
Deciding whether the average is mean, median, or mode, and what are all expected or reasonable cases can be difficult.</em>
</p>

<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorPEB">PEB</a></p>
<h2>More information</h2>
<p>
<a href="https://www.cs.uml.edu/~wang/acc-forum/" target="_blank">Average Case Complexity Forum</a>
</p>

